                of the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ball"} ball
            %li
              %p
                These spheres, or rather their underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial sets
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead%27s+theorem"} Whitehead's theorem
                says that these are all that you need; no further
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+homotopy+theory"} generalised homotopy theory
                (in a sense
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eckmann%E2%80%93Hilton+duality"} dual
                to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Steenrod+cohomology+theory"} Eilenberg–Steenrod cohomology theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+dimension+spheres+are+H-cogroup+objects"}> positive dimension spheres are H-cogroup objects
                , and this is the origin of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                structure on
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+complexity"} topological complexity
              of the sphere is
            #eq:TopologicalComplexityOfSpheres.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TC
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo ;
                            %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %mi odd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 3
                          %mtd
                            %mo ;
                            %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %mi even
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    TC
                    \\big(
                    S^n
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\begin{array}{ll}
                    2 &amp; ; n \quad odd
                    \\\
                    3 &amp; ; n \quad even
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right.
            %p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Farber01"}> Farber 01, Theorem 8
            )
          %p This proposition can be generalized:
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+complexity"} topological complexity
              of a product of spheres is
            #eq:TopologicalComplexityOfProductOfSpheres.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TC
